      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Last year's Victoria Derby winner FOX DAN (1) had some tricky draws during the Brisbane carnival but did manage a placing behind subsequent Inter Dominion winner Captains Mistress. Has had close to eight weeks off but goes very well fresh. Led to win the last time he raced in Victoria so has the speed to take full advantage of the ace draw. HESITATE (3) is another that has been freshened off the Brisbane carnival and while he didn't produce his best there he is capable when right. He could show that from this favourable draw. FAIRPLAY (5) faces a tougher test but he is progressing strongly, winning all four starts this time in. NEW SHUFFLE (9) resumes off strong form, last seen when runner-up in the City Of Melton Plate in May to follow a string of wins. Tricky draw but races well fresh and was readied with a trial. APOLLOSTORM (10) is another that cops a tough draw and steps up in grade but he deserves some respect having won four of his last five starts.",
